<!--
  The eraser: the account the nightly erasure of deleted organizations connects
  as (ADR-014, `nexovue_scheduler.erasure`), and the only one in nexovue that
  can delete telemetry (docs/changes/deployment-tells-the-truth).

  It counts what is left of each owed tenant (SELECT), deletes it
  (ALTER DELETE), and watches its own mutations in system.mutations, which
  this server version also requires a grant to read. Nothing else: no DROP, INSERT, FILE, URL or S3, which the
  administrator account it replaces held.

  Not readonly: a readonly account cannot run a mutation at all, nor send the
  `mutations_sync` setting each statement carries.
-->
<clickhouse>
  <users>
    <nexovue_eraser>
      <password from_env="CLICKHOUSE_ERASER_PASSWORD"/>
      <profile>default</profile>
      <quota>default</quota>
      <networks>
        <ip>::/0</ip>
      </networks>
      <grants>
        <query>GRANT SELECT, ALTER DELETE ON nexovue.*</query>
        <query>GRANT SELECT ON system.mutations</query>
      </grants>
    </nexovue_eraser>
  </users>
</clickhouse>
